Day 44: Flask – Routing & Templates

Topic:  
Flask routing enables mapping URLs to specific functions, while templates allow dynamic HTML generation using the Jinja2 templating engine. Dynamic routes handle variable URL patterns, and `render_template` integrates Python data with HTML for dynamic web page creation.

Learning Objectives:  
• Understand URL routing and dynamic routes in Flask.  
• Learn Jinja2 basics for HTML templating.  
• Pass data from Python to HTML templates using `render_template`.  
• Build a multi-page Flask site with navigation.  

Activities / Deliverables:  
• Create a 4-page Flask site with home, about, contact, and data pages.  
• Implement dynamic routes for handling variable URL patterns.  
• Use Jinja2 to render HTML templates with passed data.  

Important Concepts:  
• URL routing maps URLs to view functions.  
• Jinja2 templating allows dynamic HTML generation with Python data.  

SQL Syntax / Commands:  
• N/A (No SQL commands covered in this session.)  

Real-world Use Cases:  
• Building dynamic websites with Flask for small to medium-sized projects.  
• Creating reusable templates for consistent UI design across web pages.  

Tools / Tech:  
• Python  
• Flask  
• Jinja2  
• VS Code  

Summary:  
Today's session focused on Flask routing and templating, enabling the creation of dynamic web pages. We built a 4-page Flask site, implemented dynamic routes, and used Jinja2 to pass data to HTML templates, enhancing our web development skills.  

